    statement: 'Read in full: the routine obj1+0x153d8 (Ghidra FUN_000253d8, called from the race frame routine) sorts the draw list built by view.object-projection and view.player-car-draw and draws it. The list holds 0x28-byte records from obj2+0x19a50, numbered from 1 (the record 0 at obj2+0x19a28 is the swap buffer), count in the word obj2+0x28b78. It first copies the word obj2+0x1eb80 + 2 x the player index (obj2+0x28b7e) into obj2+0x28be0 (the draw switch) and sets a flag when obj2+0x28be2 or obj2+0x28bdc is non-zero (obj1+0x153de to +0x15418). The sort is a selection sort with swaps: for each record i from 1 to count - 1 and each later record j, the records are swapped, as ten dwords through the buffer (obj1+0x26f8c), when the distance dword +0x10 of i is smaller than that of j (obj1+0x15430 to +0x15484), so the list ends in falling order of distance, the farthest first, and ties keep their order. Then the routine obj1+0x12bf4 (atr.kind-effects) runs on the sorted list, and the records are drawn in list order, so near things cover far ones (obj1+0x15490 to +0x15599): the record whose number is the word obj2+0x28c12 (set by obj1+0x12bf4, one record, a car or an object) is drawn by obj1+0x14bcc; every other record is drawn only when the draw switch obj2+0x28be0 is non-zero, by putting its width, height, left column and top row into obj2+0x28b36, +0x28b26, +0x28b32 and +0x28b34, its pixel pointer into obj2+0x1d838, its frame address into obj2+0x1d704 and its skip bytes into obj2+0x1d878 and calling obj1+0x27487 (the clipped blit of sp.draw); for the second player (obj2+0x28b7e non-zero) with the flag set the top row is lowered by the word obj2+0x1ed30 first (the split screen offset). Not observed at run time.',
